  <page_number>44</page_number>
  <running_head>I. Iacomoti</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Sacuior</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Damna suis metuenda ferres.</i></p>
    <p><i>Non tutiori carcere Virginem</i><br/><i>Seruasse prudens Acrisius pater</i><br/><i>Fertur, nec audacem catena</i><br/><i>Pirithoum grauior repressit.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sed qui supremo Numine temperat</i><br/><i>Orbem, timores risit Ibericos:</i><br/><i>Custode quum iussit remoto</i><br/><i>Clastra patere tibi reclusa.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sic liberatum nunc precibus piae</i><br/><i>Gentis Nouaeum reddit amabilem:</i><br/><i>Uxoris &amp; charum redonat</i><br/><i>Fletibus egregiae maritum:</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui magna ferret commoda patriae,</i><br/><i>Qui damna pulsis adderet hostibus</i><br/><i>Dicenda, bellorum peritus</i><br/><i>Milite seu duce vellet uti,</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui sceptra Princeps Gallica sustinet.</i><br/><i>Foecunda culpae secula nobiles</i><br/><i>Odere veros, atque honore</i><br/><i>Non merito decorant inertes.</i></p>
    <p><i>Te cura Christi provida recreet</i><br/><i>Reddens solutis compedibus, noua</i><br/><i>Virtuteque auctum nunc amatis</i><br/><i>Auxilium gregibus futurum,</i></p>
    <p><i>Ardens recentis quos rabies Lupi</i><br/><i>Terret pauentes, quum stabulis malum</i><br/><i>Qua dissipatos nunc receptant</i></p>
    <p type="foot">Saevior</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The word at the lower right, "Saevior", is a catchword. Italic verse throughout; the line breaks within stanzas are marked with line breaks. Some letters are doubtful in the scan, notably "Ibericos" and "Acrisius"; the ligatures of the italic type are read as printed.</notes>
